  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nThe pattern will remain cooler and relatively wet through early\nnext week as the upper low wobbles across the Pacific \nNorthwest. A 20-60% chance of showers and 10-20% chance of \nthunderstorms will continue into Friday as the low center lifts \nto the north. Precipitation chances then decrease Saturday into \nearly Sunday as the low pivots back to the west, but will still \nremain around 10-30%. The low is then favored to move to the \neast late Sunday into Monday, increasing precipitation chances \nto 30-60% once again before decreasing Tuesday. However, \nforecast confidence is lower during this period as tropical \nactivity off the coast of Baja California will have downstream \nforecast implications. Even if tropical activity stays offshore,\nthere is potential for entrainment of tropical moisture into \nthe interior West, which would increase the risk for heavy \nrainfall. Temperatures will gradually warm to only a few degrees\nbelow normal by Saturday, then cool once again early next week \nas showers increase.",
